# Studio help documentation

Authenticated help lives at **`/studio/help`** (`src/pages/studio/help.astro`). It is linked only from `/studio` (not public nav). SWA requires `authenticated` for `/studio` and `/studio/*`. Signed-in users may open help **even when they cannot publish**.

## Keep docs in sync with capabilities

When you change Studio capabilities, update the help catalog in the same change:

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Add / rename / remove a Gemini tool in `api/src/lib/gemini.js` | Matching entry in `src/lib/studioHelp.ts` (`tool`, summary, `livePath`, `examplePrompts`) |
| Change voice UX (hold-to-speak, mic copy, browser support) | Voice section in `src/pages/studio/help.astro` + `studioVoiceNotes` in `studioHelp.ts` |
| Change compose / preview / publish flow | Getting started + Preview & publish sections on the help page |
| Change sign-in vs publish gates | Access section on the help page + publisher-gate copy on `studio.astro` |
| Replace help screenshots | `public/images/studio-help/*.jpg` — reference device is **iPhone 17 · Safari**. Current set: hub, gallery, rates, hold-to-speak, mic permission, preview, done. |

Do not invent Studio features in help that Gemini cannot perform. Example prompts must match real tools and brand rules (voice lessons only — no acting-lesson marketing).

After prompt/tool edits, follow `docs/runbooks/refine-studio-gemini.md` (includes the help-sync checklist).
